From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:55:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: ImGui's Vulkan buffers made without waiting for the
 device

ImGui's Vulkan backend waited for the whole device to be idle before it
made or grew a vertex or index buffer. PS5CEMU-HAR also draws its 3DS
menu with it, into Azahar's command buffers, while Azahar's other
threads submit to the queue, which a device-wide wait must not overlap.
A first buffer now waits for nothing, and buffers start at 1 MiB of
vertices and 512 KiB of indices, more than a menu draws, so it never
grows them. Cemu's own overlays still wait when they grow one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/imgui/imgui_impl_vulkan.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imgui/imgui_impl_vulkan.cpp b/src/imgui/imgui_impl_vulkan.cpp
index f9a2316..cf530b9 100644
--- a/src/imgui/imgui_impl_vulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/imgui/imgui_impl_vulkan.cpp
@@ -246,7 +246,16 @@ static void check_vk_result(VkResult err)
 static void CreateOrResizeBuffer(VkBuffer& buffer, VkDeviceMemory& buffer_memory, VkDeviceSize& p_buffer_size, size_t new_size, VkBufferUsageFlagBits usage)
 {
 	ImGui_ImplVulkan_InitInfo* v = &g_VulkanInitInfo;
+#if defined(CEMU_PS5)
+	// PS5CEMU-HAR also draws its 3DS menu with this, in Azahar's command buffers while Azahar's
+	// other threads use the queue: a first buffer waits for nothing, and buffers start big enough
+	// that a menu never grows them
+	if (buffer != VK_NULL_HANDLE)
+		vkDeviceWaitIdle(v->Device); // make sure previously created buffer is not in use anymore
+	new_size = std::max<size_t>(new_size, usage == VK_BUFFER_USAGE_VERTEX_BUFFER_BIT ? 1024 * 1024 : 512 * 1024);
+#else
 	vkDeviceWaitIdle(v->Device); // make sure previously created buffer is not in use anymore
+#endif
     VkResult err;
 	if (buffer != VK_NULL_HANDLE)
 		vkDestroyBuffer(v->Device, buffer, v->Allocator);
